740</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Aota</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Nomizu</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamada</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The short amino acid sequence Pro-His-Ser-Arg-Asn in human fibronectin enhances cell-adhesive function</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>1994</year><volume>269</volume><fpage>24756</fpage><lpage>24761</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7929152</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Benecky</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Kolvenbach</surname><given-names>CG</given-names></name><name><surname>Wine</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>DiOrio</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Mosesson</surname><given-names>MW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Human plasma fibronectin structure probed by steady-state fluorescence polarization: evidence for a rigid oblate structure</article-title><source>Biochemistry</source><year>1990</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>3082</fpage><lpage>3091</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2337580</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Borsi</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Carnemolla</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Catellani</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosellini</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Vecchio</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Allemanni</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Taylor-Papadimitriou</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Pande</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Zardi</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Monoclonal antibodies in the analysis of fibronectin isoforms generated by alternative splicing of mRNA precursors in normal and transformed cells</article-title><source>J Cell  Biol</source><year>1987</year><volume>104</volume><fpage>595</fpage><lpage>600</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3643927</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bowditch</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Hariharan</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Tominna</surname><given-names>EF</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamada</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Getzoff</surname><given-names>ED</given-names></name><name><surname>Ginsberg</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Identification of a novel binding site in fibronectin: differential utilization by &#x003b2;3 integrins</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>1994</year><volume>269</volume><fpage>10856</fpage><lpage>10863</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7511609</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Carnemolla</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Balza</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Siri</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Zardi</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Nicotra</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Bigotti</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Natali</surname><given-names>PG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A tumor-associated fibronectin isoform generated by alternative splicing of messenger RNA precursors</article-title><source>J Cell Biol</source><year>1989</year><volume>108</volume><fpage>1139</fpage><lpage>1148</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2646306</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Okayama</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>High-efficiency transformation of mammalian cells by plasmid DNA</article-title><source>Mol Cell Biol</source><year>1987</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>2745</fpage><lpage>2752</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3670292</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Maeda</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Sekiguchi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Sheppard</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Distinct structural requirements for interaction of the integrins &#x003b1;5&#x003b2;1, &#x003b1;v&#x003b2;5, and &#x003b1;v&#x003b2;6 with the central cell binding domain in fibronectin</article-title><source>Cell Adhes Commun</source><year>1996</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>237</fpage><lpage>250</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9117344</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Danen</surname><given-names>EHJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Aota</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>van Kraats</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamada</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruiter</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>van Muijen</surname><given-names>GNP</given-names></name></pe